    "result_text": "Owner responses now include `initials`, built from the first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, upper-cased, with a dot after each (e.g. \"john\"/\"smith\" \u2192 `J.S.`). The test suite passes: it's a single acceptance test (`coreComputesInitials`) and it runs green.\n\n**Changes:**\n- **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`**: added a read-only `initials` string to the `Owner` schema, next to the existing `displayName`. The `OwnerDto` class is generated from this file, so this is where the new field has to go.\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`**: `toOwnerDto` now fills in `initials` through a new `toInitials(owner)` helper. If a name is missing or empty, that letter is simply left out.\n\nEvery endpoint that returns an owner goes through `toOwnerDto`, so `initials` appears on get, list, create, update and delete responses alike.",
